{
 "description": "Layered equipment: the texts of the screens at the Smithy in the five game languages (RomFS folders), the words added to the look names, the cost of a look (recipes), the forge-style screens' rectangles, rows, priorities, colours and icons (forge_screen; a null is filled in when the screen opens; cursor: [frames held, rows a step] while up or down is held, at most 4, frames growing; weapon_preview_frames: the frames the cursor rests on a weapon's row before the model shows it, 1-255), and changes to the generated look lists (game/data/generated/layered_looks.json). Texts are ASCII or Latin letters only: the game's font may lack other symbols. A menu line is at most about 20 characters, a help text two lines of about 30. rank_unlocks: what opens a rank on the screens: a look shows only once its rank is open, whatever its own rule; low rank is always open, \"high\" opens the high rank looks (10325 is the Gathering Hall star 3 urgent that opens star 4; story flag 1573 is set when the Caravan girl's talk opens the Caravan star 7, the first quest of which, 701, needs only that flag), \"g\" the G rank looks (10725, the Hall star 7 urgent, opens Dundorma); an entry is a quest id (open when cleared; it must be in the game's cleared quest list) or {\"flag\": n} (open when story flag n is set); any one entry of a list opens its rank; 1 to 4 entries per rank. nothing: the armor look \"Nothing\" (the game's underwear on every part, free, first under every filter). monster_order, monster_words, monster_of: the order of the lists by monster, least to most powerful.",
